# Developer-specific env files (each dev has their own)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.claude is the docker-mcp's canonical env file: COMMITTED so the integrity
# gate can verify it against origin/main|develop (a tracked, reviewed env file is
# what stops an agent remounting host paths via *_HOST_DIR). It is machine-
# agnostic — per-machine host roots come from the docker-mcp's own env
# (HOST_REPOS_ROOT / HOST_DATA_ROOT) — and holds NO secrets (those are in
# repo-configs/secrets.env via KOALIXCRM_ENV_DIR).
!.env.claude
# Per-developer NATIVE env files (.env.aaron, .env.<name>) stay gitignored: the
# docker-mcp never uses them (it is hard-tied to .env.claude), and they carry
# machine-specific absolute paths. Do NOT commit them.

# Secrets (never commit)
secrets.env
secrets.env.local

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# mkdocs build output
site/
